shape contracts (block syntax for structured fields)
  unsupported member options
    raises a shape-member-specific (not generic unknown-key) error when a member declares as:
    raises a shape-member-specific (not generic unknown-key) error when a member declares prefix:
  declaration-time guards
    raises when a shape block is declared on a scalar type
    raises when a shape block is declared with no type
    raises when a shape block is declared on a Date (scalar) type
    raises when a shape block is declared on a union type
    accepts a shape block combined with on: (kwarg parity) and enforces the members
    still enforces the structured-type rule for a shape block under on:
    raises when a shape block is declared across multiple fields
  method_call: opt-in for object/Array-method shape members (PRO-2907)
    without the flag (safe default)
      raises MethodCallNotPermittedError reading a non-Data object member (loud, not silent)
      never mutates an element during validation (field :pop over Array elements does not run)
    with method_call: true
      resolves a non-Data object member by invoking its reader
      resolves an Array-method member by invoking it
    regression: safe members keep working with no flag
      reads Hash-key members via dig
      reads Struct members via dig
      reads OpenStruct members via dig
      reads Data members via #to_h (the axn-mcp array-element-shape-over-Data case)
    gate is independent of action threading
      raises even when an action IS present, as long as method_call was not permitted
      resolves when method_call is permitted, action present or not
    a raw shape that names no members
      rejects an absent members list
      rejects an explicit nil members list on the same terms
      names the member carrying a malformed nested shape
      accepts an explicitly empty members list
    the member snapshot
      stores axn's own ShapeConfig rather than the caller's object
      stores a String member name as its Symbol
      validates and reflects a String-keyed member bag as its canonical form
      behaves identically for the Symbol-keyed spelling
      does not let a mutated inclusion: list widen a declared member's enum
      reflects an exposes member carrying a per-validator gate, which needs a config copy
      ignores a #default reader, so the schema no longer promises a default nothing applies
    a member's shorthand validator value
      stores `type: Hash` as the bag every consumer reads
      validates `type: Hash`, which used to fail every call with `must supply :klass`
      reflects it as exactly what the `{ klass: }` spelling reflects, inbound and outbound
      projects and validates a bare `of:`, which used to take the projection down
      projects a bare `type:` carrying a nested shape, and validates through it
      expands a String-keyed bag by its canonical keys
      rejects a `validate:` Hash carrying no callable at declaration
      rejects `model:` at declaration, as the block form does
      rejects `confirmation:` at declaration, as the block form does
      rejects `of:` beside a non-Array `type:` at declaration, with the field path's own message
      rejects a bare `of:` with no `type:`, as the field path does
      rejects `of: nil` at declaration, where it used to raise on every call
      leaves `of: false` as inert on a member as it is on a field
      detaches a bare `type:` list, so mutating it cannot widen a declared member
    a member's nested `shape:`
      derives the container from the member's own `type:`, where every call used to raise TypeError
      stores the node the block form stores for the same declaration
      derives an Array container for an Array-typed member, as the field path does
      derives at every nesting level, not just the first
      rejects a non-class nested `container:` at declaration, with the field path's own message
      rejects one nested two levels down just the same
      raises when the member declares no structured `type:` to derive from
      leaves an explicit nested `container:` exactly as declared
      gives one shared nested shape the container each position calls for
      derives on the outbound route too
    a member's option keys
      rejects a typo at declaration, naming the member and the key
      rejects one two levels down just the same
      rejects a key that is not a Symbol at all
      refuses a key that claims to be a recognized one, naming it by class
      rejects optional: in the bag, pointing at where a member carries it
      rejects sensitive: in the bag, pointing at where a member carries it
      rejects user_facing: in the bag, pointing at where a member carries it
      rejects method_call: in the bag, pointing at where a member carries it
      rejects description: in the bag, pointing at where a member carries it
      gives default: the block form's own reason rather than the unknown-key message
      gives preprocess: the block form's own reason rather than the unknown-key message
      gives as: the reader-less reason
      gives prefix: the reader-less reason
      refuses a top-level `coerce:`
      refuses the `type: { coerce: true }` spelling, which used to be silently inert
      refuses one two levels down
      leaves `coerce: false` the legal no-op it is on a field
      still accepts every validation a member legitimately carries
      accepts ActiveModel's shared options, which apply on this route
      leaves a member's own attributes alone — they were never bag keys
      leaves the block form's own verdicts unchanged
    duck-typed member contract (reflection)
      reflects a member implementing only #field and #validations
      reflects such a member on exposes too
      still emits a description when the member defines one
    duck-typed member contract (member without #method_call)
      treats a member lacking #method_call as not opted in (safe default), no NoMethodError
    nested shapes inherit the rule at each depth
      raises for a method-dispatch member nested inside another shape without the flag
      resolves a nested method-dispatch member when it opts in

a shape graph a class holds that cannot be traversed
  the projection walks
    reports a bounded error on input_schema for a self-referential graph
    reports a bounded error on input_schema for a generative graph
    reports a bounded error on output_schema for a self-referential graph
    reports a bounded error on output_schema for a generative graph
    does not report a generative graph as a cycle
    names the member by class rather than reading its name
  the redaction walks
    keeps the sensitive-member predicate exact for a self-referential graph
    answers true past the depth bound, so a generative graph is masked wholesale
    keeps the candidate walk bounded for a cycle graph
    keeps the candidate walk bounded for a generative graph
    keeps inspect's own redaction walk bounded
    still settles a logged call as an ordinary result
  the mask that descends a shaped value
    masks a self-referential value wholesale where it repeats, instead of recursing
    keeps inputs_for_logging bounded on a self-referential value
    keeps the facade's inspect bounded on a self-referential value
    descends a cyclic graph as far as an acyclic value goes
    masks every position of a shared but acyclic graph
    masks a value repeated among siblings in full at both positions
    masks a cycle that closes through an array
  the validation walk that descends a shaped value
    settles a cyclic graph over a self-referential value as an ordinary result
    closes the same cycle when it runs through an Array container
    still validates every level a legal declared shape reaches into a self-referential value
    descends a cyclic graph as far as an acyclic value goes
    reports the required member of every distinct shape node one value is reached under
    validates a value repeated among siblings at both positions
    reports a bounded error for a generative graph over a self-referential value
    validates the leaf of a graph declared at the maximum depth
    leaves an ordinary nested shape validating exactly as before
  the ambient placement check
    is bounded when a later ambient subfield is declared over a cycle graph
    is bounded when a later ambient subfield is declared over a generative graph
  the bound itself
    accepts an honest graph at the cap, for declaration AND projection
    rejects one level past it at declaration
    accepts a shared-tail graph at the cap, for declaration AND projection
    logs a shared-tail graph at the cap in the clear, with no `sensitive:` declared
    rejects a graph whose depth is reached only through subtrees already verified shallower

a validate: lambda that raises an exception axn cannot describe
  settles on the validation error for an ordinary raise (control)
  settles on the validation error when the lambda's exception has a raising #message
  settles on the validation error when the lambda's exception holds unrenderable message bytes

a default:/preprocess: proc whose own raised exception axn cannot describe
  does not let result.error raise for an unrenderable default: proc failure (weak on its own)
  keeps the DefaultAssignmentError typing when the default: proc's own error has a raising #message
  keeps the PreprocessingError typing when the preprocess: proc's own error has a raising #message

validator class cache
  reuses the same compiled validator class across two calls with the same config
  builds a distinct class per coerce state for the same config
  does not reuse a class across two distinct FieldConfigs for the same field name
  invalidates when the class redeclares the field
  gives a subclass its own cache rather than inheriting the parent's

an `on:` that names a validation context
  Validation::Base.entry_context_scoped?
    reads a plain bag carrying on:
    reads a bag without on: as unscoped
    reads a non-Hash entry as unscoped
    is not fooled by a bag that denies being a Hash and hides its keys
  inside a validator's option bag
    is refused on a top-level expects, naming the field, the validator and the fix
    is refused on an exposes
    is refused on an on: subfield, whose own on: is the parent and stays legal
    is refused on a block-form shape member
    is refused through Axn::Factory.build
    is refused for on: :create
    is refused for on: nil
    is refused for on: false
    is refused for on: []
    is refused on length:
    is refused on presence:
    is refused on inclusion:
    is refused on numericality:
    is refused on format:
    is refused on of:
    is refused on validate:
    is refused on a raw shape: bag's own on:
    names every offending entry, not only the first
    is refused on a raw shape: member, which bypasses expects' option handling
    is refused on an object-backed member, which only the declaration walk sees
  what stays legal
    accepts a declaration-level on: — the subfield parent
    accepts a declaration-level on: beside a legitimately gated entry
    accepts on: :ambient_context
    accepts every other ActiveModel shared option nested in an entry
    accepts a nested strict:, which raises rather than being inert
  at the top of a shape member's bag
    is refused on a raw shape: member
    is refused on a block-form member
    keeps reporting an unknown key as unknown rather than as a context option
    keeps reporting a reader option with the reader-less reason
    still accepts the tolerance a member's bag may legitimately carry
  at the top of an exposes declaration
    is refused, naming both meanings it cannot have
    is refused whatever the value, since nothing reads it either way
    leaves an ordinary exposes untouched
    is refused even where :on has been planted in the field-metadata registry
    cannot be reached that way in the first place — registering :on is refused

Axn::Validators::OfValidator
  of: String
    passes when all elements are strings
    fails when any element is not a string
    passes for empty array (element validation is vacuous; presence is separate)
    fails for nil element (nil is not a String)
  of: Integer
    passes for integer elements
    fails for non-integer elements
  of: :boolean
    passes for true/false elements
    fails for nil element
    fails for truthy non-boolean
  of: :uuid
    passes for valid UUID strings
    fails for non-UUID strings
    fails for a blank element even when the field allows blank (allow_blank governs the field, not its elements)
  of: [String, Numeric]
    passes when elements are any of the specified types
    fails when an element matches none
    passes with empty array (element validation is vacuous)
  of: [:boolean, String]
    accepts booleans and strings
    rejects integers
  of: <Data.define class>
    passes when elements are instances of the Data class
    fails for plain hashes — is_a? check is strict
    fails for nil elements
  whole-value nil/blank handling
    with allow_nil
      skips element validation when value is nil
      still rejects a nil element inside the array
    with allow_blank
      skips element validation when value is nil
      still rejects a nil element inside the array
    with optional
      skips element validation when value is nil
      still rejects a nil element inside the array
  when value is not an Array
    does not double-report — TypeValidator owns the type error, not OfValidator
  declaration-time validation
    raises ArgumentError when of: is used without type: Array
    raises ArgumentError when type: is a union containing Array
    raises ArgumentError when of: is used without any type:
    raises ArgumentError when of: is a hash with no :klass key
  on exposes
    validates exposed array elements
    passes when exposed array elements match
  on expects with on: (subfields)
    passes when subfield array elements match
    fails when a subfield array element does not match
  error messages
    names the single expected type
    names all expected types for a union
    includes the index of each failing element
    honors a custom message: while still reporting the element index

Axn::Validators::TypeValidator
  type validation
    standalone value format
      boolean
        validates
        and allow_blank
          validates
        and allow_nil
          validates
      params
        validates
        and allow_blank
          validates
        with ActionController::Parameters
          validates ActionController::Parameters
      uuid
        validates
        and allow_blank
          validates
      class types
        validates
        and allow_blank
          validates
      array of types
        when valid
          is expected to be ok
        when invalid
          fails
        when false
          fails
        and allow_blank
          validates
    hash format with with key
      boolean
        validates
        with custom message
